# Scraper Break Fallback Guide

**Use this when the weekly GitHub Actions run fails due to the EliteProspects scraper breaking.**

---

## How to tell the scraper broke

1. Go to your repo → **Actions** tab
2. You'll see a red ❌ next to **Weekly Veteran Tracker Update**
3. Click the failed run → expand the **Build tracker** step
4. Look for an error mentioning `EliteProspects`, `scraper`, or `tdhepscrape`

If you see that, follow the steps below.

---

## Step 1 — Download current season stats from EliteProspects manually

For each league, go to the stats page on EliteProspects and download the player stats CSV.  
EP limits downloads to **100 rows at a time** so you may need multiple downloads per league.

**Naming convention — this is critical:**
```
2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (1)_nhl.csv
2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (2)_nhl.csv   ← if more than 100 players
2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (1)_ahl.csv
2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (1)_echl.csv
... etc
```

League codes to use at the end of the filename:
| League | Code |
|--------|------|
| NHL | `_nhl` |
| AHL | `_ahl` |
| ECHL | `_echl` |
| KHL | `_khl` |
| SHL | `_shl` |
| Finnish Liiga | `_liiga` |
| Czech Extraliga | `_czechia` |
| Slovak Extraliga | `_slovakia` |
| German DEL | `_del` |
| Swiss NL | `_nl` |

Save all files into your local `25_26_updated_stats/` folder.

---

## Step 2 — Run the preprocessing script locally

Open a terminal in the folder where `prepare_manual.py` lives and run:

```bash
python prepare_manual.py
```

**What it does:**
- Reads all CSVs from `25_26_updated_stats/`
- Detects league from filename
- Merges multi-part files (the 100-row batches)
- Matches players to their EliteProspects links using the historical data
- Outputs two files into a `manual/` folder:
  - `current_season.csv` — the file you'll upload to GitHub
  - `unmatched_players.csv` — players it couldn't match (spot check these)

**Expected output:**
```
Found 12 CSV file(s) in '25_26_updated_stats/':
  ✅  2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (1)_echl.csv  →  echl
  ✅  2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (2)_echl.csv  →  echl
  ...

Building player name → EP link lookup...
  Built lookup with 14,000+ unique player keys.

Processing ECHL (2 file(s))...
  Matched: 87/113 (77%)   Unmatched: 26 (23%)
...
✅  Wrote manual/current_season.csv
⚠️  Wrote 84 unmatched players → manual/unmatched_players.csv
```

> **Note on unmatched players:** First-year pros won't be in the historical data —
> this is expected and fine. They'll show in the app as under-threshold which is accurate.
> Only worry if you spot-check `unmatched_players.csv` and see recognizable veterans.

---

## Step 3 — Upload to GitHub

1. Go to your GitHub repo → click into the `manual/` folder
2. Click **Add file** → **Upload files**
3. Upload `current_season.csv` (from your local `manual/` folder)
4. Click **Commit changes**

---

## Step 4 — Trigger a manual Actions run

1. Go to your repo → **Actions** tab
2. Click **Weekly Veteran Tracker Update** in the left panel
3. Click **Run workflow** → **Run workflow**
4. Wait for the green ✅ (2–5 minutes)

The script will:
1. Try the scraper → fail
2. Detect `manual/current_season.csv` → use it instead
3. Rebuild the site normally

The live site header will show **"Manual data load"** instead of the update date
so you know it's running on manual data.

---

## Step 5 — When the scraper is fixed

Once the scraper is working again (usually after a TopDownHockey package update):

1. Go to your repo → `manual/` folder
2. Click `current_season.csv` → click the **trash icon** → **Commit changes**
3. Trigger a manual Actions run to confirm the scraper works

The site will go back to fully automatic weekly updates.

---

## Local folder structure reminder

Your local machine should look like this when running the fallback:

```
prepare_manual.py
25_26_updated_stats/
  2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (1)_echl.csv
  2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (2)_echl.csv
  2025-2026 Regular Season Player Stats (1)_ahl.csv
  ... etc
data/
  nhl_career_1516_2425.csv
  ahl_career_1516_2425.csv
  echl_career_1516_2425.csv
  ... (all 10 historical CSVs downloaded from GitHub)
manual/
  current_season.csv        ← generated by prepare_manual.py
  unmatched_players.csv     ← review this
```

